---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, BASE, stats, categories, abs } from '../lib/catalog';

const base = BASE;
---

<Base
  title="About, attribution & how the archive was built"
  description="How the Parkjets Archive was built, what it contains, how aircraft designs and photography are credited, and how to add a new aircraft."
  canonical={abs('/about')}
  image="/og-default.png"
>
  <Shell>
    <main id="main" class="page">
      <header class="page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">Project</p>
        <h1 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:60ms">About this archive</h1>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
          Parkjets Archive is an independent, non-commercial preservation of the RC parkjet and
          park flyer plan catalogue originally published at
          <a href={SITE.sourceSite} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{SITE.sourceSite.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
          It exists so that the catalogue, its designer credits and its build knowledge survive a
          change of hosting.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="layout">
        <article class="prose-col">
          <!-- ------------------------- contents ------------------------- -->
          <section id="contents" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">§</span> On this page</h2>
            <ul class="contents">
              <li><a href="#what">What this archive contains</a></li>
              <li><a href="#attribution">Attribution &amp; rights</a></li>
              <li><a href="#plans">Why plan files are links, not downloads</a></li>
              <li><a href="#method">How the migration was done</a></li>
              <li><a href="#quality">Data quality &amp; what is missing</a></li>
              <li><a href="#adding">Adding a new aircraft</a></li>
              <li><a href="#technical">Technical notes</a></li>
              <li><a href="#privacy">Privacy</a></li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <!-- --------------------------- what --------------------------- -->
          <section id="what" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">01</span> What this archive contains</h2>
            <p>
              Every published entry in the Parkjets plan collection was imported:{' '}
              <strong class="mono">{stats.aircraft}</strong> aircraft in total. For each one the
              archive preserves:
            </p>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li>The catalogue name, the designer's credit and the source categories.</li>
              <li>Every specification the designer published, kept in their own words, alongside a machine-readable subset.</li>
              <li>The designer's notes, recommended build items and any links they published.</li>
              <li>Build-thread and reference links to the original sources.</li>
              <li>All <span class="mono">{stats.images}</span> gallery photographs, re-hosted locally at two resolutions.</li>
              <li>A permanent link to the original Parkjets product page.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              The catalogue taxonomy is taken verbatim from the source:{' '}
              {categories.map((c) => c.value).join(', ')}.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- ----------------------- attribution ------------------------ -->
          <section id="attribution" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">02</span> Attribution &amp; rights</h2>
            <div class="callout">
              <p><strong>Project code</strong> and <strong>archived content</strong> are licensed differently.</p>
            </div>
            <h3>Project code — MIT</h3>
            <p>
              The website, build tooling, validation scripts and documentation in this repository
              are released under the MIT licence. See <code>LICENSE</code>.
            </p>
            <h3>Archived content — not ours to license</h3>
            <p>
              The aircraft designs, plan files, specifications, notes and photographs are{' '}
              <strong>not</strong> covered by the repository licence. They remain the intellectual
              property of the individual designers and photographers who created them, and of
              Parkjets. This project asserts no redistribution right over them; it preserves them
              for reference and always credits the author on every page.
            </p>
            <p>
              Parkjets and the individual designers are free to ask for any archived item to be
              removed; see the contact details below.
            </p>
            <h3>Photography</h3>
            <p>
              Aircraft photographs are credited to the contributors named in the original image
              descriptions and to Parkjets for hosting. Copies stored here are reduced-resolution
              and exist for identification and reference.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- --------------------------- plans -------------------------- -->
          <section id="plans" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">03</span> Why plan files are links, not downloads</h2>
            <p>
              Parkjets published its plan files as member-only digital goods. They were released
              only to accounts signed in to the Parkjets membership, and there is no public,
              unauthenticated download address for them. That access control is a deliberate
              commercial decision by the site owner and this project respects it.
            </p>
            <p>
              Rather than present download buttons that would not work, every aircraft page shows
              one of two honest states, driven by a real check of what is stored in the repository:
            </p>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li><span class="chip chip--ok">Archived</span> — a validated copy of the file lives in this repository and downloads directly from this site.</li>
              <li><span class="chip chip--warn">Source only</span> — the entry, imagery and the original filename are archived; the file itself is fetched from the original product page.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              If the site owner later releases any plan files for redistribution, dropping them into{' '}
              <code>public/plans/&lt;slug&gt;/</code> is all that is required — the next build will
              validate them and the button changes itself.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- -------------------------- method -------------------------- -->
          <section id="method" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">04</span> How the migration was done</h2>
            <p>
              The catalogue was read from the public, machine-readable representation the source
              site already publishes for its own product grid, cross-checked against the site's{' '}
              <code>sitemap.xml</code> and against every category page. The three sources agree
              exactly, which is how we know nothing is missing or duplicated.
            </p>
            <p>The pipeline lives in <code>scripts/</code> and is reproducible:</p>
            <ol class="steps">
              <li><code class="mono">npm run discover</code> — inventory the collection, categories and URLs.</li>
              <li><code class="mono">npm run import</code> — build <code class="mono">data/aircraft.json</code>.</li>
              <li><code class="mono">npm run assets</code> — download and validate every photograph.</li>
              <li><code class="mono">npm run archive</code> — locate, validate and checksum any plan files; write the archive manifest.</li>
              <li><code class="mono">npm run validate</code> — refuse to build if anything is inconsistent.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout">
              <p>
                The importer never invents data. A specification is only recorded when the designer
                literally wrote it. Where the source is silent, the page says so, and where the
                designer's own wording is ambiguous it is reproduced verbatim rather than
                reinterpreted.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- -------------------------- quality ------------------------- -->
          <section id="quality" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">05</span> Data quality &amp; what is missing</h2>
            <p>
              This is a preservation of a hand-written catalogue, so the record is uneven by nature.
              Known limitations, all of them inherited from the source rather than introduced here:
            </p>
            <ul class="ticks ticks--warn">
              <li>
                <span class="mono">{stats.aircraft - stats.specifications}</span> of{' '}
                <span class="mono">{stats.aircraft}</span> designs were published without
                structured specifications. Those pages show the designer's text verbatim instead.
              </li>
              <li>Some entries were never credited to a designer. The archive records the absence rather than guessing.</li>
              <li>Several distinct designs share a name because they are different builds of the same airframe by different modellers. Those are kept as separate entries and disambiguated by designer.</li>
              <li>Plan files are member-gated at the source and are therefore not mirrored here.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              A machine-readable migration report is published at{' '}
              <a href={SITE.repo + '/blob/main/reports/migration-report.md'} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                reports/migration-report.md
              </a>{' '}
              in the repository.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- -------------------------- adding -------------------------- -->
          <section id="adding" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">06</span> Adding a new aircraft</h2>
            <p>No code changes are required. Four steps:</p>
            <ol class="steps">
              <li>
                Add one object to <code>data/aircraft.json</code> with the fields shown in the
                file's existing entries (<code>slug</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>designer</code>,{' '}
                <code>category</code>, <code>specifications</code>, <code>sourceUrl</code>, …).
              </li>
              <li>
                Drop photographs into <code>public/media/aircraft/&lt;slug&gt;/</code> as{' '}
                <code>01-400.webp</code> / <code>01-1200.webp</code> and reference them in the
                entry's <code>images</code> array.
              </li>
              <li>
                If a plan file may be redistributed, place it in{' '}
                <code>public/plans/&lt;slug&gt;/</code> keeping its original filename.
              </li>
              <li>
                Run <code class="mono">npm run validate &amp;&amp; npm run build</code>, then commit
                and push. GitHub Actions rebuilds the site and the new aircraft appears
                automatically, in the catalogue, in search, in the filters and in the sitemap.
              </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="muted">
              The validator will fail the build if the slug is duplicated, an image is missing, a
              local download is broken, or an internal link points nowhere.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- ------------------------ technical ------------------------- -->
          <section id="technical" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">07</span> Technical notes</h2>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li>Fully static output. No server, no database, no Squarespace code of any kind.</li>
              <li>Search and filtering run entirely in the browser over the pre-rendered catalogue, so the site is usable with JavaScript disabled.</li>
              <li>No analytics, no trackers, no cookies, no third-party scripts beyond a webfont stylesheet.</li>
              <li>Animations are CSS plus a small dependency-free observer script, and every one of them is disabled under <code class="mono">prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</li>
              <li>Every archived file is checksummed; the audit trail is <code class="mono">data/archive-manifest.json</code>.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <!-- -------------------------- privacy -------------------------- -->
          <section id="privacy" class="dsec" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="dsec-title"><span class="mono">08</span> Privacy</h2>
            <p>
              This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads no advertising. The only
              external request it can make is for the webfont, served by Google Fonts, when your
              browser does not already have it cached.
            </p>
          </section>
        </article>

        <aside class="side">
          <section class="panel panel--pad" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="side-title">Source &amp; contact</h2>
            <dl class="kv">
              <div><dt>Original site</dt><dd><a class="link" href={SITE.sourceSite} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{SITE.sourceSite.replace('https://', '')} ↗</a></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Plan collection</dt><dd><a class="link" href={SITE.sourceCollection} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">/free-plans ↗</a></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Repository</dt><dd><a class="link" href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener" target="_blank">github.com ↗</a></dd></div>
              <div><dt>Contact</dt><dd><a class="link" href={'mailto:' + SITE.contactEmail}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a></dd></div>
            </dl>
          </section>

          <section class="panel panel--pad" data-reveal>
            <h2 class="side-title">Archive at a glance</h2>
            <dl class="kv">
              <div><dt>Aircraft</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.aircraft}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Designers credited</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.designers}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Categories</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.categories}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Photographs</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.images}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>With specifications</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.specifications}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Build threads linked</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.buildThreads}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Plans archived</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.archived}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Source-only</dt><dd class="mono">{stats.sourceOnly}</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </section>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </main>
  </Shell>
</Base>

<script>
  import '../scripts/motion.js';
</script>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 1.2rem + 3vw, 3.5rem) 1rem;
  }
  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-block: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 70ch;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 2.5vw, 3rem);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 20rem);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .prose-col {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.75rem, 1.4rem + 1.5vw, 2.75rem);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .dsec-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .dsec-title .mono {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .prose-col p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .prose-col h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose-col code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--cyan) 10%, transparent);
    color: var(--cyan);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .contents {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 230px), 1fr));
  }
  .contents a {
    display: block;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .contents a:hover {
    color: var(--cyan);
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }
  .ticks {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .ticks li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .ticks li::before {
    content: '▸';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .ticks--warn li::before {
    content: '△';
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .steps {
    counter-reset: step;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem 0.7rem 2.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink-700) 40%, transparent);
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.9rem;
    top: 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .callout {
    padding: 0.9rem 1.05rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--cyan);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--cyan) 8%, transparent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .callout p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .side {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 1rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .side-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .kv {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.05rem;
  }
  .kv > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--line-soft) 60%, transparent);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .kv > div:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .kv dt {
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding-top: 0.16rem;
  }
  .kv dd {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .kv dd.mono {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .link {
    color: var(--cyan);
    /* WCAG 2.5.8 — these links are the whole content of their <dd>. */
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: 0.24rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .side {
      position: static;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
